<h2>Category Analysis by Trade: Specific Recommendations for Plumbers, HVAC, Electricians, and Roofers</h2>

<p>Generic advice fails because every trade has different category options, seasonal patterns, and customer search behavior. Here is what the data says for the four most common home service trades.</p>

<h3>Plumbers: The Data on Primary and Secondary Categories</h3>

<p>Of the 412 plumbing profiles we analyzed, the most common primary categories were "Plumber" (67%), "Plumbing Service" (18%), and "Emergency Plumbing Service" (12%). The data showed a clear winner.</p>

<p>Businesses using "Plumber" as their primary category ranked an average of 2.1 positions higher than those using "Plumbing Service" for the keyword "plumber near me." The difference was even starker for "Emergency Plumbing Service": businesses with that primary category ranked 4.3 positions higher for "emergency plumber" searches but 3.7 positions lower for generic "plumber" searches.</p>

<p><strong>Primary category recommendation:</strong> Use "Plumber" unless emergency work represents 70%+ of your revenue. If you are 24/7 emergency-focused, "Emergency Plumbing Service" is worth the tradeoff for generic visibility.</p>

<p><strong>Secondary category stack (ranked by impact):</strong></p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Drain Cleaning Service</strong> - Appeared in 34% of top-3 Map Pack results for "drain cleaning"</li>
<li><strong>Water Heater Installation/Repair</strong> - High search volume, low competition in most markets</li>
<li><strong>Pipe Repair Service</strong> - Captures burst pipe and leak searches</li>
<li><strong>Sewer Service</strong> - Strong for "sewer line replacement" queries</li>
<li><strong>Septic System Service</strong> - Essential if you offer septic work; irrelevant otherwise</li>
<li><strong>Emergency Plumbing Service</strong> - Add as secondary if not your primary</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Case study:</strong> A plumbing business in Knoxville, Tennessee switched from "Plumbing Service" to "Plumber" and added "Drain Cleaning Service," "Water Heater Installation," and "Pipe Repair Service" as secondary categories. Over 11 weeks, their Map Pack position for "plumber Knoxville" moved from 8 to 4, then to 1 after review velocity improvements. Profile views increased 340%, direction requests increased 280%, and phone calls increased 190%.</p>

<h3>HVAC Contractors: Seasonal Strategy Drives Results</h3>

<p>HVAC had the most complex category dynamics of any trade we studied. The primary category decision depends heavily on your business model and season.</p>

<p>Businesses using "HVAC Contractor" as a year-round primary category ranked an average of 5.2 for "HVAC near me" but 9.8 for "air conditioning repair" in summer and 10.1 for "furnace repair" in winter. Businesses that switched seasonally averaged 4.1 for "HVAC near me" (slightly better due to perceived specialization) and 3.2 for seasonal keywords.</p>

