<p><strong>Warning:</strong> Do not add "Plumber" as a secondary category even if you do some plumbing work. Our data showed HVAC businesses with "Plumber" as a secondary category ranked an average of 1.8 positions lower for HVAC keywords. The relevance dilution is real when categories cross trades.</p>

<h3>Electricians: Specificity Beats Generality</h3>

<p>Of the 298 electrical profiles analyzed, 71% used "Electrician" as their primary category. The remaining 29% used variants like "Electrical Contractor," "Electrical Installation Service," or specialty categories like "Solar Energy Company."</p>

<p>The data was unambiguous. "Electrician" outperformed "Electrical Contractor" by 1.7 positions on average for "electrician near me." "Electrical Installation Service" performed well for "electrical installation" (2.3 positions better than "Electrician") but poorly for generic electrician searches (4.1 positions worse).</p>

<p><strong>Primary category recommendation:</strong> Use "Electrician" unless you exclusively perform a specialty. If you are solar-only, "Solar Energy Company" is correct. If you are 90% residential electrical work, "Electrician" wins.</p>

