<h2>Attribute Analysis: Which GBP Attributes Actually Move the Needle</h2>

<p>Attributes are the most underutilized ranking signal in Google Business Profiles. While categories tell Google what you do, attributes tell Google how you do it and who you serve. Our analysis shows that attribute completion is not just a completeness checkbox. It is a direct ranking factor.</p>

<h3>How Attributes Influence Rankings</h3>

<p>Google uses attributes in three ways. First, as filter criteria. When a user searches for "wheelchair accessible plumber," only profiles with the "Wheelchair-accessible entrance" attribute appear. Second, as relevance signals. A profile with "Free estimates," "Online appointments," and "Onsite services" sends stronger service-intent signals than a bare profile. Third, as AI Overview fuel. Google's AI-generated answers for local queries pull directly from attribute data.</p>

<p>Our data showed that profiles with 76-100% attribute completion ranked 2.3 positions higher than profiles with 0-25% completion. The effect was consistent across all 12 trades, though the magnitude varied.</p>

<h3>High-Impact Attributes by Category</h3>

<p>Not all attributes are equal. We grouped attributes by type and measured their correlation with ranking improvement.</p>

