<p>Service options and offerings showed the strongest correlation. This makes sense: these attributes directly answer user intent. When someone searches for "plumber free estimate," the "Free estimates" attribute is a direct match.</p>

<h3>Identity Attributes: The Surprising Performance Data</h3>

<p>Identity-based attributes like "Women-led," "Veteran-owned," and "Black-owned" showed a smaller but consistent positive correlation. Businesses with at least one identity attribute ranked 0.8 positions higher on average. The mechanism is not entirely clear, but two factors likely contribute.</p>

<p>First, Google has explicitly stated that it surfaces these attributes in search results and filters. Searches for "black-owned business" increased over 600% in one year, and Google created dedicated filters for these attributes. Second, identity attributes may increase click-through rate, which feeds back into ranking algorithms through behavioral signals.</p>

<p><strong>Important:</strong> Only add identity attributes that are true and verifiable. Google has suspended profiles for false identity claims.</p>

<h3>The Predefined Services Revolution</h3>

<p>In 2025, Google rolled out predefined services for more categories. Instead of manually typing "drain cleaning," plumbers can now select "Drain Cleaning" from a dropdown that Google recognizes as a structured entity. This matters because predefined services match exact search queries with higher confidence than custom text.</p>

<p>Our analysis found that profiles using predefined services for their core offerings ranked 1.1 positions higher than profiles using only custom services. The effect was strongest when the predefined service exactly matched the search query.</p>

<p><strong>Action step:</strong> Log into your GBP dashboard, go to the Services section, and select every predefined service that applies to your business. Then add custom services for anything not covered by predefined options.</p>

<h3>Attributes and AI Overviews</h3>

<p>With 40% of local business queries now triggering Google AI Overviews, attributes have become even more critical. Google's AI pulls structured data from GBP to generate answers like "Here are three plumbers in Atlanta who offer free estimates and 24/7 emergency service." If your profile lacks those attributes, you do not get mentioned.</p>

<p>Businesses with complete attribute profiles were 2.7x more likely to be referenced in AI Overview answers for their target keywords. This is a new ranking dimension that did not exist two years ago.</p>

